      timeline: [
        '1940s: Game originated in South America',
        '1990s: Became immensely popular in Italy',
        '1990s-present: Federazione Italiano Burraco established; rules standardized',
        '2000s-present: Active tournament scene and competitive leagues',
      ],
      evolution: 'The Italian version standardized rules that were more variable in South American versions. Key differences from Brazilian Buraco include the dealing method (cutting and forming pozzetti differently) and specific card values.',
      cultural: 'Burraco is one of the most popular card games in Italy, played in homes, clubs, and competitive tournaments. The Federazione Italiano Burraco organizes national championships and maintains official rules.',
    },
